+    exactly once. An independent uniform shuffle does so only in expectation:
+    the probability that k draws from k positions are all distinct is k!/k**k, so
+    for k = 6 the probability that at least one member STILL has no position-1
+    observation after 6 experiments is 1 - 6!/6**6 = 0.98456790123457. Exact
+    coverage dominates coverage-in-expectation on the named property, and is the
+    simpler mechanism.
 
+    THIS IS NOT A RANKING AND MAKES NO CAPABILITY CLAIM. A rotation preserves a
+    sequence's membership and its cyclic successor relation and asserts nothing
+    about which member is stronger. It is applied ONLY where
+    `strength_order_from_evidence` has already declined to establish an order.
